 "transcript": [
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son, the second son): \"Why do you not come in to your father and eat a little food?\"",
  "the eldest son (to the second son): \"We have been to the officer's house, father, and the young wife is a most beautiful woman, and she has given me a silver knife and a silver mirror and a pair of silver chopsticks, and it was she who gave me the silver knife, and it is she who gave me the mirror and the chopsticks.\"",
  "[silence] Wang Lung says nothing.",
  "[action] (to Wang Lung) The eldest son takes the silver knife and looks at it.",
  "[action] (to the second son) The eldest son looks at the silver chopsticks and mirror.",
  "[silence] Wang Lung says nothing.",
  "[action] Wang Lung turns to his sons.",
  "[action] The eldest son looks at his brother with a scowl.",
  "[says] (to Wang Lung) Eldest son complains about his younger brother's plans.",
  "[action] Wang Lung listens to his son's complaints.",
  "[action] (to Wang Lung) The eldest son looks at his father with contempt.",
  "[action] Wang Lung avoids meeting his son's eyes.",
  "[action] (to Wang Lung) The second son approaches his father, bowing deeply.",
  "the second son (to Wang Lung): \"Aye, and I can see that we are to be left out and I am not to have any of the gold and silver that my brother would have in his hands. For if the land is sold, it is no longer land but money, and the land in the hands of a man is worth more than the land in my hands. I wish I had had the land. It was mine by right, even as the land of my father.\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"No, and you are not to have it!\"",
